From 17c7254f80916ae0d650e269ce9476a54e31c1e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 11:55:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mission: spray and COMPLETED gated only on raw GNSS radial <=
 30 mm

RPP still stops the rover and certifies its 20 mm estimator-frame stop
exactly as before; its along/cross/overall numbers are now debug report
only. After the stop, mission_manager measures raw RTK-FIXED GNSS
(post-stop fixes only, >=3 samples over 1.0 s, cluster scatter <= 20 mm)
against the surveyed coordinate. Radial <= 30 mm -> spray + COMPLETED;
> 30 mm, or no trustworthy measurement within 3.0 s -> FAILED, no spray.
The verdict is one-shot and is the survey block stored in the report.

An RPP MISSED with RADIAL20_SETTLED_OUTSIDE_TOLERANCE (a proven settled
stop) is also decided by raw GNSS; every other MISSED reason still fails
directly. Survey targets must carry the loaded mission's path signature.

spray_controller independently re-checks the gate from mission status
(run/point bound, radial and tolerance <= its own 30 mm limit) before
PRESS and aborts to release if it is lost mid-spray.

